.TH tunumfmt n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tunumfmt
.PP
\fBnumfmt\fR\-like human\-readable number formatting in pure Tcl (SI and IEC).
.SS API
.CS
::tclutils::tunumfmt::toHuman   number ?-to si|iec? ?-precision N?
::tclutils::tunumfmt::fromHuman string ?-from si|iec|auto?
::tclutils::tunumfmt::text      text   ?-mode to|from? ?...?
::tclutils::tunumfmt::file      path   ?-mode to|from? ?...?
.CE
.PP
\fBtoHuman\fR scales a number to a unit suffix (SI uses 1000, IEC 1024), e.g. \fB1500\fR becomes \fB1.5K\fR and \fB1536 \-to iec\fR becomes \fB1.5Ki\fR. \fBfromHuman\fR parses such strings back; \fB\-from auto\fR treats an \fBi\fR right after the unit letter as IEC, so \fB2Ki\fR and \fB2KiB\fR are 2048 while \fB2K\fR and \fB2KB\fR are 2000. Default precision is 1 decimal; values below the first unit are emitted as integers.
.SS CLI
.CS
printf '1500\n1048576\n' | tclsh bin/tunumfmt.tcl
tclsh bin/tunumfmt.tcl -mode from sizes.txt
.CE
